From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noswad <64293615+TheNoswad@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 20:20:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: max77759: charge at 500 mA from Default USB
 sources

tcpm gives CURRENT_MAX=0 for a Default-Rp source when the TCPC has no
BC1.2, so the charger never turned its buck on from a PC port.
---
 drivers/power/supply/max77759_charger.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/max77759_charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/max77759_charger.c
index 62f9e23d6..4fc3b0b95 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/max77759_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/max77759_charger.c
@@ -619,6 +619,14 @@ static void psy_work_item(struct work_struct *work)
 		goto err;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * tcpm reports 0 for a Default-USB-power source (plain PC port or
+	 * USB-A charger) when the TCPC has no BC1.2 detection, which would
+	 * leave the buck off. Fall back to the USB 2.0 default of 500 mA.
+	 */
+	if (online.intval && !current_limit.intval)
+		current_limit.intval = 500000;
+
 	if (online.intval && current_limit.intval) {
 		ret = set_input_current_limit(chg, current_limit.intval);
 		if (ret) {
